> How does one play with tiles but without the GUI features?

     The MSDOS version can switch between text and tiles
using function buttons (F2 and F3?  I don't remember...) and
uses the same basic interface either way.  For Windows, the
text-only version (nethack.exe) and the one that can show
either tiles or text (nethackW.exe) are two separate programs,
and the latter uses a Windows-style mouse interface both ways.
So with it, "You can't get there from here."

> If that isn't possible. Can the "features" be disabled in the source
> before compiling?

     No, the two Windows versions use separate code rather
than alternate configuration of common code.  Try downloading
the MSDOS binaries instead of the Windows package.  It runs
under Windows (at least for variants prior to Vista; I'm not sure
about Vista and Windows 7 or whatever the new one is called).

> The Windows interface is beyond annoying, especially the intermittent
> OK/Cancel buttons that must be clicked. I much prefer the "cleaner"
> tty interface, but it doesn't load my tiles from default.nh.

     You could probably type Enter to pick OK and Esc to
pick Cancel, without resorting to the mouse.  Also, adding
OPTIONS=3Dmenustyle:traditional to your configuration file will
bypass popup menus for operations like the 'D' command that
let you choose multiple inventory items.


